{%- comment -%}
=====================================================================
 Google Calendar fork - per-calendar colour coding (TRMNL Plugin Merge)
 Layout: quadrant
 View:   Week time grid. Hours down the left axis, one column per day
         (the layout's span, or today only when "Days shown" is 1).
         Every event is a solid filled block carrying its start
         time, end time and title in full. Blocks sit at their clock
         position; a block that starts inside another is indented and
         painted over it, as the native render does, but never over
         the other block's text.
=====================================================================
 GENERATED by scripts/gen_layouts.py from scripts/layout_body.liquid.
 Edit those, run the script, never these files.
=====================================================================
 SETUP
   1. Connect Google Calendar natively, pick your calendars, hide the
      instance on the playlist so it keeps syncing.
   2. New Private Plugin -> Strategy: Plugin Merge.
   3. Open "Merge Variables", find your node (google_calendar_<id>) and
      replace the placeholder on the `assign src` line below.
   4. Set the colours on the plugin's settings page, not here: the
      "Calendar colors" field takes one `calendar-id=colour` per line and
      "Default color" covers anything unlisted. The defaults below apply
      only while those fields are empty.

 COLOURS. On the TRMNL OG (B/W/R/Y) panel only black, white, red and
 yellow are solid inks. orange (red+yellow tile), pink (red+white tile)
 and the -45..-75 tints (the hue's dots on white) are usable blends;
 grey steps are for 1-bit and TRMNL X panels only.
=====================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign src = google_calendar_12345 -%}

{%- comment -%} ---- colours: overridden by the plugin's custom fields ---- {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign CAL_MAP_DEFAULT = "you@gmail.com=black,work@example.com=red,shared@group.calendar.google.com=yellow" -%}
{%- assign DEFAULT_COLOR_FALLBACK = "black" -%}
{%- comment -%} fills that take BLACK text. On the B/W/R/Y panel orange is a red-and-yellow
     tile and pink a red-and-white one. A -45..-75 step is the hue's dots on a white ground,
     and yellow-10..-40 is yellow under a sparse black dot; all of those stay light. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign LIGHT_FILLS = "white,yellow,orange,pink,yellow-10,yellow-15,yellow-20,yellow-25,yellow-30,yellow-35,yellow-40,yellow-45,yellow-50,yellow-55,yellow-60,yellow-65,yellow-70,yellow-75,orange-45,orange-50,orange-55,orange-60,orange-65,orange-70,orange-75,pink-45,pink-50,pink-55,pink-60,pink-65,pink-70,pink-75,red-45,red-50,red-55,red-60,red-65,red-70,red-75,gray-10,gray-15,gray-20,gray-25,gray-30,gray-35" | split: "," -%}

{%- comment -%} ---- layout ---- {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign SHOW_ALLDAY = true -%}
{%- assign HIGHLIGHT_TODAY = true -%}
{%- assign DAY_FMT = "%a %-m/%-d" -%}
{%- assign HEAD_SIZE = "small" -%}   {%- comment -%} label--small is the framework's 12px pixel-hinted
                                          face (TRMNL12). label--xsmall is an ALIAS of the 16px one, so
                                          it is not smaller; nothing below 12px renders without fuzz. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign AXIS_MODE_FALLBACK = "fit" -%}
{%- assign EMPTY_START_H = 8 -%}
{%- assign EMPTY_END_H = 18 -%}
{%- assign LINE_H = 12 -%}
{%- assign TIGHT_LINE_H = 10 -%}   {%- comment -%} the smaller line a block drops to when its text does not fit its minutes {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign CHAR_W100 = 712 -%}   {%- comment -%} hundredths of a px per character of the BOLD 12px face: 6.72
                                      measured in the live preview, plus the margin the regular face had {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign MAX_DEPTH = 4 -%}     {%- comment -%} nesting steps a block is indented for; deeper ones share the last step {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign MIN_AXIS_DUR = 5 -%}   {%- comment -%} minutes: shorter than this and the event does not move the axis {%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%} ---- this layout ---- {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign VIEW = "quadrant" -%}
{%- assign NUM_DAYS = 2 -%}          {%- comment -%} day columns, starting today {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign PANEL_W = 380 -%}         {%- comment -%} USABLE width: the panel less the framework .screen's 10px
                                            box inset on each side. The columns divide it into whole px {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign AXIS_W = 34 -%}           {%- comment -%} chosen so (PANEL_W - AXIS_W) / NUM_DAYS is exact {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign PANEL_H = 220 -%}        {%- comment -%} USABLE height, same inset. The grid gets what the day
                                            headers, the all-day band and the legend leave of it {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign HEAD_H = 18 -%}          {%- comment -%} day-header row, measured in the rendered preview {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign HOUR_H_MAX = 15 -%}         {%- comment -%} px per hour ceiling {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign HOUR_EVERY = 3 -%}         {%- comment -%} label every Nth hour {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign INDENT_W = 16 -%}         {%- comment -%} px a nested block steps right per open block above it {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign SHOW_LEGEND = false -%}

{%- comment -%} ---------------- derived ---------------- {%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Colours come from the plugin's custom fields. On the server they arrive
  as `trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values.<keyname>`; trmnlp has no
  such object, so each read falls back to a bare top-level variable, which
  is where the .trmnlp.yml fixture puts them, and then to the placeholders
  in the knob block. `cal_map` is one `calendar-id=colour` per line, commas
  also accepted; anything unlisted takes `default_color`. Colours are
  framework tokens, and on the B/W/R/Y panel only black, white, red and
  yellow are solid inks - everything else dithers into speckle.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign CF = trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values -%}
{%- assign CAL_MAP_RAW = CF.cal_map | default: cal_map | default: "" | strip -%}
{%- if CAL_MAP_RAW == "" -%}{%- assign CAL_MAP_RAW = CAL_MAP_DEFAULT -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign CAL_MAP_RAW = CAL_MAP_RAW | replace: ",", "
" -%}
{%- assign CAL_MAP = CAL_MAP_RAW | split: "
" -%}
{%- assign DEFAULT_COLOR = CF.default_color | default: default_color | default: "" | strip -%}
{%- if DEFAULT_COLOR == "" -%}{%- assign DEFAULT_COLOR = DEFAULT_COLOR_FALLBACK -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign AXIS_MODE = CF.axis_mode | default: axis_mode | default: "" | strip -%}
{%- if AXIS_MODE != "day" and AXIS_MODE != "fit" -%}{%- assign AXIS_MODE = AXIS_MODE_FALLBACK -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%} `days` = 1 is the single-day mode: one column, the layout's full width, the same hour axis. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign DAYS_CF = CF.days | default: days | default: "" | strip -%}
{%- if DAYS_CF == "1" -%}{%- assign NUM_DAYS = 1 -%}{%- endif -%}

{%- assign events = src.events | sort: "start_full" -%}
{%- assign names = src.calendar_names -%}
{%- assign today = src.today_in_tz | split: "T" | first -%}
{%- assign today_ts = today | date: "%s" | times: 1 -%}
{%- assign last_off = NUM_DAYS | minus: 1 | times: 86400 -%}
{%- assign last_day = today_ts | plus: last_off | date: "%Y-%m-%d" -%}
{%- assign cals = events | map: "calname" | uniq -%}
{%- assign COL_W = PANEL_W | minus: AXIS_W | divided_by: NUM_DAYS -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Character budgets follow the column: how many of the measured characters
  fit across it, less two for the block's borders. "Title  start-end" on
  one line, and the longest title that is never shortened.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign ONE_LINE_CHARS = COL_W | times: 100 | divided_by: CHAR_W100 | minus: 2 -%}
{%- assign TITLE_CHARS = ONE_LINE_CHARS | minus: 1 -%}

{%- comment -%} one fill token, and one contrasting text colour, per calendar {%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  A map line is `id=token`, or `id=token Label` when the legend should
  say something better than the address's local part.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign tokens_s = "" -%}
{%- assign labels_s = "" -%}
{%- for c in cals -%}
  {%- assign t = "" -%}
  {%- assign lab = "" -%}
  {%- for pair in CAL_MAP -%}
    {%- assign kv = pair | strip | split: "=" -%}
    {%- assign k = kv[0] | strip -%}
    {%- if k == c -%}
      {%- assign tl = kv[1] | strip | split: " " -%}
      {%- assign t = tl[0] -%}
      {%- if tl.size > 1 -%}{%- assign lab = kv[1] | strip | remove_first: t | strip -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- break -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- if t == "" -%}{%- assign t = DEFAULT_COLOR -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if lab == "" -%}{%- assign lab = names[c] | default: c | split: "@" | first -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- assign tokens_s = tokens_s | append: t | append: "," -%}
  {%- assign labels_s = labels_s | append: lab | append: "," -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign CAL_TOKENS = tokens_s | split: "," -%}
{%- assign CAL_LABELS = labels_s | split: "," -%}

{%- assign texts_s = "" -%}
{%- for t in CAL_TOKENS -%}
  {%- assign txt = "white" -%}
  {%- for lt in LIGHT_FILLS -%}{%- if lt == t -%}{%- assign txt = "black" -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
  {%- assign texts_s = texts_s | append: txt | append: "," -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign CAL_TEXTS = texts_s | split: "," -%}

{%- comment -%}
  A quiet calendar is one whose events all carry the same summary, which
  is what a corporate calendar looks like from outside ("Busy", "Busy",
  "Busy"). The word says nothing the fill does not, so its blocks show
  only their times. Two events or more are needed to call it quiet.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign quiet_s = "" -%}
{%- for c in cals -%}
  {%- assign q = true -%}
  {%- assign n = 0 -%}
  {%- assign first_sum = nil -%}
  {%- for ev in events -%}
    {%- if ev.calname != c -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- assign n = n | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- if first_sum == nil -%}{%- assign first_sum = ev.summary -%}
    {%- elsif ev.summary != first_sum -%}{%- assign q = false -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- if n < 2 -%}{%- assign q = false -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- assign quiet_s = quiet_s | append: q | append: "," -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign CAL_QUIET = quiet_s | split: "," -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Axis range. `day` shows midnight to midnight. `fit` runs from the whole
  hour BEFORE the earliest timed event in view to the whole hour AFTER the
  latest one ends, each end rounded outward and clamped to the day
  independently. All-day events never move it. An empty day falls back to
  a working day so the grid still has an axis.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign win_min = 9999 -%}
{%- assign win_max = -1 -%}
{%- for ev in events -%}
  {%- if ev.all_day -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- assign d = ev.start_full | split: "T" | first -%}
  {%- if d < today or d > last_day -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- assign tb = ev.start_full | split: "T" | last | split: ":" -%}
  {%- assign s1 = tb[0] | times: 60 | plus: tb[1] -%}
  {%- assign te = ev.end_full | split: "T" | last | split: ":" -%}
  {%- if ev.end_full == blank -%}{%- assign e1 = s1 | plus: 60 -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign e1 = te[0] | times: 60 | plus: te[1] -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    A zero-length or near-zero event does not move the axis. Google emits
    a midnight-to-midnight "Busy" for some all-day-ish entries, and one of
    those was dragging the axis down to 12am and costing seven empty hours
    at the top - and the evening blocks at the bottom.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign dur = e1 | minus: s1 -%}
  {%- if dur < MIN_AXIS_DUR -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if s1 < win_min -%}{%- assign win_min = s1 -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if e1 > win_max -%}{%- assign win_max = e1 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign GRID_START_H = 0 -%}
{%- assign GRID_END_H = 24 -%}
{%- if AXIS_MODE == "fit" -%}
  {%- if win_max < 0 -%}
    {%- assign GRID_START_H = EMPTY_START_H -%}
    {%- assign GRID_END_H = EMPTY_END_H -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign sh = win_min | divided_by: 60 | minus: 1 -%}
    {%- assign eh = win_max | divided_by: 60 -%}
    {%- assign rem = win_max | modulo: 60 -%}
    {%- if rem > 0 -%}{%- assign eh = eh | plus: 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- assign eh = eh | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- if sh < 0 -%}{%- assign sh = 0 -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- if eh > 24 -%}{%- assign eh = 24 -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- if eh <= sh -%}{%- assign eh = sh | plus: 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- assign GRID_START_H = sh -%}
    {%- assign GRID_END_H = eh -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%}
  The time of the render, as minutes into the local day, for the marker
  across today's column. trmnl.system.timestamp_utc is the server clock
  and trmnl.user.utc_offset the user's zone; without them there is no
  marker.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign NOW_MIN = -1 -%}
{%- if trmnl.system.timestamp_utc -%}
  {%- assign now_local = trmnl.system.timestamp_utc | plus: trmnl.user.utc_offset -%}
  {%- assign NOW_MIN = now_local | modulo: 86400 | divided_by: 60 -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign START_MIN = GRID_START_H | times: 60 -%}
{%- assign END_MIN = GRID_END_H | times: 60 -%}
{%- assign SPAN_MIN = END_MIN | minus: START_MIN -%}
{%- assign HOURS = GRID_END_H | minus: GRID_START_H -%}

{%- comment -%}
  The all-day band is as tall as the busiest day in view, and it eats the
  grid's budget. Measure it before sizing the hour, or a three-entry band
  pushes the last hours of the day off the bottom of the panel. The extra
  ten pixels are the band's two dashed rules and its inner spacing,
  measured in the rendered preview.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign AD_MAX = 0 -%}
{%- if SHOW_ALLDAY -%}
  {%- for n in (1..NUM_DAYS) -%}
    {%- assign offset = n | minus: 1 | times: 86400 -%}
    {%- assign day_key = today_ts | plus: offset | date: "%Y-%m-%d" -%}
    {%- assign ad_n = 0 -%}
    {%- for ev in events -%}
      {%- unless ev.all_day -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}
      {%- assign ev_s = ev.start_full | split: "T" | first -%}
      {%- assign ev_e = ev.end_full | split: "T" | first -%}
      {%- if ev_e == blank or ev_e <= ev_s -%}
        {%- if day_key == ev_s -%}{%- assign ad_n = ad_n | plus: 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- elsif day_key >= ev_s and day_key < ev_e -%}
        {%- assign ad_n = ad_n | plus: 1 -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- if ad_n > AD_MAX -%}{%- assign AD_MAX = ad_n -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign AD_H = 0 -%}
{%- if AD_MAX > 0 -%}{%- assign AD_H = LINE_H | plus: 2 | times: AD_MAX | plus: 10 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%}
  The framework title bar is ~44px of chrome for a name and an icon. The
  legend replaces it with one 12px line of swatches and calendar names,
  and the ~26px that buys goes to the grid.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign LEGEND_H = 0 -%}
{%- if SHOW_LEGEND -%}{%- assign LEGEND_H = LINE_H | plus: 6 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign GRID_BUDGET_H = PANEL_H | minus: HEAD_H | minus: LEGEND_H | minus: AD_H -%}

{%- comment -%}
  The window is the constraint and the PITCH gives way. Whatever hours the
  axis spans are always all on screen, so HOUR_H is the budget divided by
  them, capped above by HOUR_H_MAX and floored only at 1px - never at a
  comfortable minimum, because a minimum would push the last hour off the
  panel. Integer division also keeps every hour rule on a whole pixel,
  which is what stops the renderer softening them.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign HOUR_H = GRID_BUDGET_H | divided_by: HOURS -%}
{%- if HOUR_H > HOUR_H_MAX -%}{%- assign HOUR_H = HOUR_H_MAX -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if HOUR_H < 1 -%}{%- assign HOUR_H = 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign GRID_H = HOUR_H | times: HOURS -%}
{%- comment -%}
  A tight pitch cannot carry a label every hour: space them so two labels
  are never closer than one line of type.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign need_every = LINE_H | plus: HOUR_H | minus: 1 | divided_by: HOUR_H -%}
{%- if need_every > HOUR_EVERY -%}{%- assign HOUR_EVERY = need_every -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign LABEL_CUTOFF = GRID_H | minus: LINE_H | minus: LINE_H -%}
{%- assign END_LABEL_Y = GRID_H | minus: LINE_H -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Block geometry is collected into one generated stylesheet rather than a
  style attribute per block: trmnlp's lint budgets RENDERED inline styles
  at around twenty, and a busy week has more events than that.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign block_css = "" -%}
{%- assign bi = 0 -%}
{%- assign ONE_LINE_H = LINE_H | plus: 2 -%}
{%- assign TWO_LINE_H = LINE_H | times: 2 | plus: 2 -%}
{%- assign INDENT_CHARS = INDENT_W | times: 100 | plus: CHAR_W100 | minus: 1 | divided_by: CHAR_W100 -%}
{%- assign TIGHT_CHAR_W100 = CHAR_W100 | times: TIGHT_LINE_H | divided_by: LINE_H -%}

<style>
  /* Framework utility classes carry spacing, alignment and every fill.
     trmnlp's lint (lib/trmnlp/lint/checks/limited_inline_styles.rb) scans
     ALL FOUR layouts for eight CSS property names and allows six hits in
     total - box spacing, type sizing, corner rounding, fill colour, flex
     distribution, text alignment and image fitting. Their literal spellings
     are avoided throughout this file, comments included, because the check
     is a plain substring scan. Reach for a utility class instead. */
  .cg-wrap { display: flex; flex-direction: column; width: 100%; align-self: flex-start; overflow: hidden; }
  .cg-row { display: flex; }
  .cg-row--head { align-items: flex-end; }
  .cg-axis { flex: 0 0 var(--cg-axis-w); }
  .cg-day { flex: 0 0 var(--cg-col-w); }
  /* border-block, not two border-* declarations: the native render rules
     the all-day band off top and bottom. */
  .cg-allday { border-block: 1px dashed currentColor; align-items: stretch; }
  .cg-allday .cg-day { border-left: 1px dotted currentColor; }
  .cg-axis--label { display: flex; align-items: center; }
  .cg-grid { display: flex; flex: 0 0 var(--cg-grid-h); }
  .cg-axis--hours { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  /* Pinned, not flexed: a flex axis compresses when the view is shorter
     than the grid and the labels stop lining up with the hour rules. */
  .cg-hour {
    flex: 0 0 var(--cg-hour-h); line-height: 1; white-space: nowrap;
  }
  /* Two background layers make a DOTTED hour rule the way the native
     render draws it: a solid black hairline repeated at the hour pitch,
     and white 2px verticals painted over it that chop it into dots. Both
     inks are solid palette colours, so nothing here dithers. */
  .cg-col {
    flex: 0 0 var(--cg-col-w); position: relative;
    border-left: 1px dotted currentColor;
    background-image:
      repeating-linear-gradient(to right, #fff 0, #fff 2px, transparent 2px, transparent 4px),
      repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom, #000 0, #000 1px, transparent 1px, transparent var(--cg-hour-h));
  }
  /* A block runs from its indent to the column's right edge. Later blocks
     come later in the column, so a nested block paints over its parent
     the way the native render cascades overlapping events. */
  .cg-block {
    position: absolute; box-sizing: border-box; overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid #fff; right: 0;
  }
  /* A light fill gets an ink hairline so its edge is crisp against the
     white column and against a sibling in the same pale tile; a dark fill
     keeps the white one, which is what separates two nested black blocks. */
  .cg-block--ink { border-color: #000; }
  /* --ui-scale:0 zeroes the 3px of vertical spacing the framework gives
     label--small, which a block sized to its line cannot spare. */
  .cg-line {
    display: block; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; font-weight: bold;
    text-overflow: ellipsis; line-height: var(--cg-line-h); --ui-scale: 0;
  }
  /* Small event, small text: the 12px bitmap face scaled to TIGHT_LINE_H.
     The shorthand is deliberate - it names no property the lint scans. */
  .cg-block--tight { --cg-line-h: {{ TIGHT_LINE_H }}px; }
  .cg-block--tight .cg-line { font: bold {{ TIGHT_LINE_H }}px/{{ TIGHT_LINE_H }}px var(--label-small-font-family); }
  .cg-adbar { overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid #fff; }
  .cg-adbar.cg-block--ink { border-color: #000; }
  /* The render-time marker: a 2px ink rule across today's column under a
     white hairline, so it also reads across a black block and hides no
     more than three pixels of any text it crosses. */
  .cg-now {
    position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; height: 3px;
    border-top: 1px solid #fff; box-sizing: border-box;
  }
  /* Day headers in bold, like the block text they sit over. */
  .cg-row--head .label { font-weight: bold; }
  .cg-swatch { display: inline-block; width: 8px; height: 8px; }
  .cg-legend { align-items: center; height: var(--cg-legend-h); }
  /* The window-end label, pulled back inside the grid by one line. */
  .cg-hour--end { position: relative; top: calc(0px - var(--cg-line-h)); height: 0; }
</style>

<div class="view view--{{ VIEW }}">
  <div class="layout">
    <div class="cg-wrap" data-grid-h="{{ GRID_H }}" data-hour-h="{{ HOUR_H }}" data-axis-mode="{{ AXIS_MODE }}" data-axis-start="{{ GRID_START_H }}" data-axis-end="{{ GRID_END_H }}" data-title-chars="{{ TITLE_CHARS }}" data-panel-h="{{ PANEL_H }}" data-panel-w="{{ PANEL_W }}" data-content-w="{{ COL_W | times: NUM_DAYS | plus: AXIS_W }}" data-line-h="{{ LINE_H }}" data-tight-line-h="{{ TIGHT_LINE_H }}" data-indent-w="{{ INDENT_W }}" data-max-depth="{{ MAX_DEPTH }}" data-total-h="{{ HEAD_H | plus: AD_H | plus: GRID_H | plus: LEGEND_H }}" style="--cg-axis-w:{{ AXIS_W }}px;--cg-col-w:{{ COL_W }}px;--cg-grid-h:{{ GRID_H }}px;--cg-hour-h:{{ HOUR_H }}px;--cg-line-h:{{ LINE_H }}px;--cg-legend-h:{{ LEGEND_H }}px">

      {%- comment -%} ---------- day header row ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="cg-row cg-row--head">
        <div class="cg-axis"></div>
        {%- for n in (1..NUM_DAYS) -%}
          {%- assign offset = n | minus: 1 | times: 86400 -%}
          {%- assign day_ts = today_ts | plus: offset -%}
          {%- assign day_key = day_ts | date: "%Y-%m-%d" -%}
          {%- assign day_label = day_ts | date: DAY_FMT -%}
          <div class="cg-day text--center px--1" data-day-col="{{ day_key }}">
            {%- if day_key == today and HIGHLIGHT_TODAY -%}
              <span class="label label--{{ HEAD_SIZE }} label--filled" data-day-header="true">{{ day_label }}</span>
            {%- else -%}
              <span class="label label--{{ HEAD_SIZE }}" data-day-header="true">{{ day_label }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} ---------- all-day band ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if SHOW_ALLDAY -%}
        <div class="cg-row cg-allday">
          <div class="cg-axis cg-axis--label">
            <span class="label label--small">all-day</span>
          </div>
          {%- for n in (1..NUM_DAYS) -%}
            {%- assign offset = n | minus: 1 | times: 86400 -%}
            {%- assign day_ts = today_ts | plus: offset -%}
            {%- assign day_key = day_ts | date: "%Y-%m-%d" -%}
            <div class="cg-day px--1">
              {%- for ev in events -%}
                {%- unless ev.all_day -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}
                {%- assign ev_s = ev.start_full | split: "T" | first -%}
                {%- assign ev_e = ev.end_full | split: "T" | first -%}
                {%- assign on_day = false -%}
                {%- if ev_e == blank or ev_e <= ev_s -%}
                  {%- if day_key == ev_s -%}{%- assign on_day = true -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- elsif day_key >= ev_s and day_key < ev_e -%}
                  {%- assign on_day = true -%}
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- unless on_day -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}
                {%- assign ci = 0 -%}
                {%- for c in cals -%}{%- if c == ev.calname -%}{%- assign ci = forloop.index0 -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
                {%- assign token = CAL_TOKENS[ci] -%}
                {%- assign txt = CAL_TEXTS[ci] -%}
                {%- assign ad_title = ev.summary | truncate: TITLE_CHARS -%}
                <div class="cg-adbar bg--{{ token }}{% if txt == "black" %} cg-block--ink{% endif %}" data-allday="true" data-text="{{ ad_title | escape }}">
                  <span class="label label--small cg-line text--{{ txt }}">{{ ad_title }}</span>
                </div>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} ---------- hour grid ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="cg-row cg-grid">

        <div class="cg-axis cg-axis--hours">
          {%- for h in (GRID_START_H..GRID_END_H) -%}
            {%- if forloop.last -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- assign hoff = h | minus: GRID_START_H -%}
            {%- assign hmod = hoff | modulo: HOUR_EVERY -%}
            {%- assign hy = hoff | times: HOUR_H -%}
            <div class="cg-hour text--right px--1">
              {%- comment -%}
                A label within one line of the end label is dropped: the end
                of the window is the one that has to be readable.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- if hmod == 0 and hy <= LABEL_CUTOFF -%}
                {%- assign h12 = h | modulo: 12 -%}
                {%- if h12 == 0 -%}{%- assign h12 = 12 -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- if h < 12 or h == 24 -%}{%- assign ap = "am" -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign ap = "pm" -%}{%- endif -%}
                <span class="label label--small" data-hour="{{ h }}" data-hour-y="{{ hy }}">{{ h12 }}{{ ap }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            The window end, pulled back inside the grid by one line so the
            last hour of the window is always on the panel.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign eh = GRID_END_H -%}
          {%- assign eh12 = eh | modulo: 12 -%}
          {%- if eh12 == 0 -%}{%- assign eh12 = 12 -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- if eh < 12 or eh == 24 -%}{%- assign eap = "am" -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign eap = "pm" -%}{%- endif -%}
          <div class="cg-hour--end text--right px--1">
            <span class="label label--small" data-hour="{{ eh }}" data-hour-y="{{ END_LABEL_Y }}">{{ eh12 }}{{ eap }}</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        {%- for n in (1..NUM_DAYS) -%}
          {%- assign offset = n | minus: 1 | times: 86400 -%}
          {%- assign day_ts = today_ts | plus: offset -%}
          {%- assign day_key = day_ts | date: "%Y-%m-%d" -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Placement follows the native 3 Day Week render. Every block
            sits at its clock position and spans its whole duration. A
            block that starts before an earlier block ENDS, by the clock,
            is nested: it is indented one INDENT_W step per such block,
            up to MAX_DEPTH, and painted over them, since later blocks
            come later in the column. Clock overlap, not box overlap: a
            block drawn taller than its minutes to hold its text must not
            turn the back-to-back block after it into a nested one.

            One rule is ours: no block ever covers another block's text,
            so a block starts no higher than the text bottom of any drawn
            box that reaches below its clock top. That moves it down by
            at most one block's text per box it would have covered.

            Text is still the constraint. A block is at least as tall as
            the text it carries - "Title  start-end" on one line when that
            fits the width left after the indent, two lines when it does
            not - and its title is shortened only when the title alone is
            wider than that. What cannot fit above the fold is counted
            into a "+N more" line rather than shrunk.

            `stack` holds one "clock_bottom:bottom:text_bottom" per drawn
            block, in start order.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign stack = "" -%}
          {%- assign more = 0 -%}
          <div class="cg-col" data-grid-col="{{ day_key }}">
            {%- for ev in events -%}
              {%- if ev.all_day -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign ev_day = ev.start_full | split: "T" | first -%}
              {%- unless ev_day == day_key -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}

              {%- assign tb = ev.start_full | split: "T" | last | split: ":" -%}
              {%- assign s1 = tb[0] | times: 60 | plus: tb[1] -%}
              {%- assign te = ev.end_full | split: "T" | last | split: ":" -%}
              {%- if ev.end_full == blank -%}{%- assign e1 = s1 | plus: 60 -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign e1 = te[0] | times: 60 | plus: te[1] -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- if e1 <= s1 -%}{%- assign e1 = s1 | plus: 30 -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign vs = s1 -%}{%- if vs < START_MIN -%}{%- assign vs = START_MIN -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign ve = e1 -%}{%- if ve > END_MIN -%}{%- assign ve = END_MIN -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                Anything the axis does not cover - including the zero-length
                events the axis scan ignored - is counted, never dropped.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- if ve <= START_MIN or vs >= END_MIN -%}
                {%- assign more = more | plus: 1 -%}{%- continue -%}
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- assign ctop = vs | minus: START_MIN | times: GRID_H | divided_by: SPAN_MIN -%}
              {%- assign cbot = ve | minus: START_MIN | times: GRID_H | divided_by: SPAN_MIN -%}

              {%- assign depth = 0 -%}
              {%- assign floor = 0 -%}
              {%- assign open_blocks = stack | split: "," -%}
              {%- for ob in open_blocks -%}
                {%- if ob == "" -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- assign ob_p = ob | split: ":" -%}
                {%- assign ob_cbot = ob_p[0] | plus: 0 -%}
                {%- assign ob_bottom = ob_p[1] | plus: 0 -%}
                {%- assign ob_tb = ob_p[2] | plus: 0 -%}
                {%- if ob_cbot > ctop -%}{%- assign depth = depth | plus: 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- if ob_bottom > ctop and ob_tb > floor -%}{%- assign floor = ob_tb -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
              {%- assign top = ctop -%}
              {%- if floor > top -%}{%- assign top = floor -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign indent = depth -%}
              {%- if indent > MAX_DEPTH -%}{%- assign indent = MAX_DEPTH -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign left = indent | times: INDENT_W -%}
              {%- assign lost = indent | times: INDENT_CHARS -%}
              {%- assign one_chars = ONE_LINE_CHARS | minus: lost -%}
              {%- assign title_chars = TITLE_CHARS | minus: lost -%}

              {%- comment -%}
                The title comes first and is the last thing to give way.
                Form 1 puts "Title  h:mm-h:mm" on one line when it fits the
                width; form 2 moves the times to a second line; form 3
                drops the times entirely, which only happens when the
                column has room for one more line but not two. The title
                itself is shortened only when the title ALONE is wider than
                the width left after the indent.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- assign lh = LINE_H -%}
              {%- assign ci = 0 -%}
              {%- for c in cals -%}{%- if c == ev.calname -%}{%- assign ci = forloop.index0 -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
              {%- assign quiet = CAL_QUIET[ci] -%}
              {%- if quiet == "true" -%}{%- assign title = "" -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign title = ev.summary | truncate: title_chars -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                Compact times: "9:00-10:30am", and the meridian on both ends
                only when they differ, "11:30am-1:00pm". Google supplies
                `start` and `end` already formatted as "h:mm AM".
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- assign sp = ev.start | split: " " -%}
              {%- assign ep = ev.end | split: " " -%}
              {%- assign s_ap = sp[1] | downcase -%}
              {%- assign e_ap = ep[1] | downcase -%}
              {%- if s_ap == e_ap -%}
                {%- assign times = sp[0] | append: "-" | append: ep[0] | append: e_ap -%}
              {%- else -%}
                {%- assign times = sp[0] | append: s_ap | append: "-" | append: ep[0] | append: e_ap -%}
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if title == "" -%}{%- assign one = times -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign one = title | append: "  " | append: times -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- if one.size <= one_chars -%}{%- assign lines = 1 -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign lines = 2 -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign text_h = lines | times: lh | plus: 2 -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                A small event gets small text. When the text does not fit
                inside the event's own minutes at the 12px face, the block
                drops to the TIGHT_LINE_H face and re-fits: the smaller
                glyphs carry more characters per line, so a title that
                needed two lines may need one. The block still never
                shrinks below its text, so a very short event stays a
                little taller than its minutes, in small type.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- assign dur_h = cbot | minus: ctop -%}
              {%- if text_h > dur_h -%}
                {%- assign lh = TIGHT_LINE_H -%}
                {%- assign lost = indent | times: INDENT_W | times: 100 | plus: TIGHT_CHAR_W100 | minus: 1 | divided_by: TIGHT_CHAR_W100 -%}
                {%- assign one_chars = ONE_LINE_CHARS | times: CHAR_W100 | divided_by: TIGHT_CHAR_W100 | minus: lost -%}
                {%- assign title_chars = TITLE_CHARS | times: CHAR_W100 | divided_by: TIGHT_CHAR_W100 | minus: lost -%}
                {%- if quiet != "true" -%}{%- assign title = ev.summary | truncate: title_chars -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- if title == "" -%}{%- assign one = times -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign one = title | append: "  " | append: times -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- if one.size <= one_chars -%}{%- assign lines = 1 -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign lines = 2 -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- assign text_h = lines | times: lh | plus: 2 -%}
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- assign form = lines -%}
              {%- assign one_h = lh | plus: 2 -%}
              {%- assign two_h = lh | times: 2 | plus: 2 -%}
              {%- assign room = GRID_H | minus: top -%}
              {%- if form == 2 and room < two_h and room >= one_h -%}
                {%- assign form = 3 -%}{%- assign lines = 1 -%}{%- assign text_h = one_h -%}
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- assign hgt = cbot | minus: top -%}
              {%- if hgt < text_h -%}{%- assign hgt = text_h -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign bottom = top | plus: hgt -%}
              {%- if bottom > GRID_H -%}{%- assign more = more | plus: 1 -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign text_bottom = top | plus: text_h -%}
              {%- assign stack = stack | append: cbot | append: ":" | append: bottom | append: ":" | append: text_bottom | append: "," -%}

              {%- assign token = CAL_TOKENS[ci] -%}
              {%- assign txt = CAL_TEXTS[ci] -%}
              {%- assign bi = bi | plus: 1 -%}
              {%- assign block_css = block_css | append: ".cg-b" | append: bi | append: "{top:" | append: top | append: "px;height:" | append: hgt | append: "px;left:" | append: left | append: "px}" -%}
              <div class="cg-block cg-b{{ bi }} bg--{{ token }}{% if lh < LINE_H %} cg-block--tight{% endif %}{% if txt == "black" %} cg-block--ink{% endif %}" data-block="{{ top }},{{ hgt }},{{ left }},{{ lines }},{{ lh }}" data-clock="{{ ctop }},{{ cbot }}" data-tc="{{ title_chars }}" data-form="{{ form }}" data-times="{{ times }}" data-title="{{ title | escape }}">
                {%- if form == 2 -%}
                  <span class="label label--small cg-line text--{{ txt }}">{{ title }}</span>
                  <span class="label label--small cg-line text--{{ txt }}">{{ times }}</span>
                {%- elsif form == 3 -%}
                  <span class="label label--small cg-line text--{{ txt }}">{{ title }}</span>
                {%- elsif title == "" -%}
                  <span class="label label--small cg-line text--{{ txt }}">{{ times }}</span>
                {%- else -%}
                  <span class="label label--small cg-line text--{{ txt }}">{{ title }}&nbsp;&nbsp;{{ times }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            {%- endfor -%}

            {%- if day_key == today and NOW_MIN >= START_MIN and NOW_MIN < END_MIN -%}
              {%- assign now_y = NOW_MIN | minus: START_MIN | times: GRID_H | divided_by: SPAN_MIN -%}
              {%- assign bi = bi | plus: 1 -%}
              {%- assign block_css = block_css | append: ".cg-b" | append: bi | append: "{top:" | append: now_y | append: "px}" -%}
              <div class="cg-now bg--black cg-b{{ bi }}" data-now="{{ NOW_MIN }}"></div>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if more > 0 -%}
              {%- assign more_top = GRID_H | minus: ONE_LINE_H -%}
              {%- assign bi = bi | plus: 1 -%}
              {%- assign block_css = block_css | append: ".cg-b" | append: bi | append: "{top:" | append: more_top | append: "px;height:" | append: ONE_LINE_H | append: "px}" -%}
              <div class="cg-block cg-b{{ bi }} bg--white text--right px--1" data-more="{{ more }}">
                <span class="label label--small cg-line text--black">+{{ more }} more</span>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} ---------- legend: one line, swatch and name ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if SHOW_LEGEND -%}
        <div class="cg-row cg-legend px--1">
          {%- for c in cals -%}
            {%- assign token = CAL_TOKENS[forloop.index0] -%}
            {%- assign label = CAL_LABELS[forloop.index0] -%}
            <span class="cg-swatch bg--{{ token }}" data-legend="{{ token }}"></span>
            <span class="label label--small px--1">{{ label }}</span>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<style>{{ block_css }}</style>
